  {
   "id": "crush-variables-md-6",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "### Type hints\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-variables-4",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "let age: Int = 30\nlet score: Float = 95.5\nlet message: String = \"Hello\"\nlet flag: Bool = true\nprint(age)\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/variables.md:38",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "30\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-variables-md-8",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "The initial value is checked against the hint at compile time\n(`let x: Int = \"s\"` is rejected). The hint is **not** re-checked on later\nassignment today.\n\n## Assignment\n\nReassign with `=`:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-variables-5",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "let counter = 0\ncounter = counter + 1\ncounter = counter + 1\nprint(counter)\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/variables.md:59",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "2\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-variables-md-10",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "Compound assignment (`+=`, `-=`, `*=`, `/=`) and `++`/`--` are **not implemented**:\nuse `counter = counter + 1`. Assigning to a name that was never declared is a\ncompile error (`Undefined variable`).\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-variables-6",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn main() {\n    counter += 1\n}\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "expected-failure"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/variables.md:76",
      "browser": "fail",
      "why": "this example shows a compile error"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-variables-md-12",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "Variables are dynamically typed at run time, so a `let`-declared name can later\nhold a value of a different type (unless the compiler can see the mismatch for a\nhinted parameter or initialiser).\n\n## Scoping rules\n\n### Function scope\n\nVariables declared in a function are local to it, and parameters are local copies:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-variables-7",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn bump(n) {\n    n = n + 1\n    return n\n}\n\nlet v = 1\nprint(bump(v))\nprint(v)\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/variables.md:90",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "2\n1\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-variables-md-14",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "Arrays and objects are passed **by reference**, so a function can mutate its\nargument in place:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-variables-8",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn add_nine(items) {\n    items.push(9)\n}\n\nlet xs = [1]\nadd_nine(xs)\nprint(xs)\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/variables.md:110",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "[1, 9]\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-variables-md-16",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "Using a function's local outside it is a compile error:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-variables-9",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn example() {\n    let x = 10\n    print(x)\n}\n\nfn main() {\n    example()\n    print(x)\n}\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "expected-failure"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
