   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-variables-md-18",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "### Module-level variables are not visible inside functions\n\nTop-level statements form the program's entry body, **not** a shared global\nscope. A function cannot read a variable declared at the top level — pass it as\nan argument:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-variables-10",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn get_level() {\n    return LEVEL\n}\n\nfn main() {\n    let LEVEL = \"production\"\n\n    print(get_level())\n}\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "expected-failure"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/variables.md:144",
      "browser": "fail",
      "why": "this example shows a compile error"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-variables-11",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "let level = \"production\"\n\nfn describe(l) {\n    return \"running in \" + l\n}\nprint(describe(level))\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/variables.md:153",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "running in production\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-variables-md-21",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "(If you need shared state across functions today, thread it through parameters,\nor keep it in an object/array you pass around.)\n\n### Block scope\n\nA name first declared inside an `if`, `while` or `for` body is not visible after\nthe block ends. A `for` loop variable is likewise local to the loop:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-variables-12",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn main() {\n    if true {\n        let y = 2\n    }\n    print(y)\n}\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "expected-failure"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/variables.md:176",
      "browser": "fail",
      "why": "this example shows a compile error"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-variables-13",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn main() {\n    for i in 0..3 {\n        print(i)\n    }\n    print(i)\n}\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "expected-failure"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/variables.md:184",
      "browser": "fail",
      "why": "this example shows a compile error"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-variables-md-24",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "### Shadowing\n\n**Across functions** a local simply hides nothing — each function has its own\nvariables:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-variables-14",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "let x = 10\n\nfn show() {\n    let x = 20\n    print(x)\n}\n\nshow()\nprint(x)\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/variables.md:196",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "20\n10\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-variables-md-26",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "**Within one function**, re-declaring an outer name in an inner block does *not*\ncreate a new shadowing variable; it assigns to the outer one. After this program\nthe outer `x` is `2`:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-variables-15",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "let x = 1\nif true {\n    let x = 2\n}\nprint(x)\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/variables.md:218",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "2\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-variables-md-28",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "Choose distinct names for inner variables rather than relying on shadowing.\n\n## Exporting a variable\n\n`export name` marks an already-declared variable or function for export. See\n[Syntax](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/syntax.html#imports-and-exports); importing it from another file is not\npossible yet (crush-ast **CRUSH-110**).\n\n## Best practices\n\n- Initialise at declaration and keep scopes narrow.\n- Pass state explicitly: functions can't see top-level variables.\n- Prefer new names over shadowing.\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- **[Operators](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/operators.html)**\n- **[Control Flow](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/control_flow.html)**\n- **[Functions](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/functions.html)**\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  }
 ]
